{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'recovery|one.effect|counter|retained|stdo-work' /Users/jim/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"55:- “Memory is an artifact of prior computation whose retained differences modify the space of subsequent transformations.” “Data is the distinguishable residue of prior computation, embodied in a form that can condition subsequent computation.” [Task 1]\n77:- GTL, ABG, STDO, formal model, candidate-only projection, qualified view, continuation-sensitive preservation, complete presentation environment, retained terms, fixed-Γ, typed annotations\n82:- The case establishes fixed-Γ preservation and ordinary statefulness, not emergence. A resolver proof must quantify over the complete presentation environment, including retained terms and qualified references, not merely historical assets. [Task 1]\n164:- symptom: a user encounters a paywall after a test was described as free, or receives a score framed as diagnosis/probability -> cause: free scoring was conflated with paid interpretation and thresholds were overread -> fix: lead with the free/paid distinction, do not diagnose from AQ/RMET, and recommend qualified assessment only for longstanding traits affecting daily functioning. [Task 3]\n190:- Forward-task repair is supported within sampled scope: `product/worksite_command_forward.ts` admits candidates through `admitJson` and compares `canonicalEquals`; sparse, undefined, and mismatching candidates throw `TypeError`, while dense and foreign-realm dense controls pass. The 867-row census is 846 retyped, 20 merged, one structural—sampled, not exhaustive. D12 admits foreign-realm plain records/arrays but rejects class instances and specified prototype counterexamples. [Task 1]\n271:- when the user says “theres nothing on the laptop that cant be recovered” -> focus on repair assessment, fees, depot/onsite logistics, and coverage rather than repeatedly foregrounding data recovery. [Task 1]\n357:- Candidate checkpoint `c29b2be37f9a12e050478be97793927d99c01781` had bounded evidence (63 dispositions, 89 members, 30/30 assertions, T2 replay 6/6), but same-family/non-author evidence, context fit, owner decisions, installed qualification, C3 acceptance, and release were open. The locked successor reader fixed counter controls but did not retroactively qualify original attempts. [Task 1]\n358:- The common archive passed bounded custody/portable verification and exact recovery, but remained locally reviewable with `semantic_acceptance: not_issued`, `publication: not_performed`, actual-use unperformed, and HTML interaction unverified. [Task 2]\n416:- E11 occurs when a Writer loses only its claim marker: a changed body/policy with the same Product/principal/request ID can receive the old success. Bind complete original request, Product/principal, and policy identity before claim/replay/recovery; missing stable owner history returns `history_incomplete`, never fresh planning or writing. [Task 1]\n459:# Task Group: ABIogenesis T-287 retained-installed consumer preparation and RC1 qualification boundary\n461:scope: Use when resuming T-287/GOAL-035 from a handoff, repairing installed consumer/preparation and historical recovery, or reporting exactly what remains before RC1 qualification.\n474:## Task 2: Repair retained-installed consumer/preparation and historical recovery, success\n478:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T15-14-42-7gWO-abiogenesis_consumer_reuse_repair_accepted_rc1_open.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T01-14-42-01a0edbb-7c4f-7493-bf06-2a600644bbb6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T02:00:55+00:00, thread_id=01a0edbb-7c4f-7493-bf06-2a600644bbb6, independently accepted bounded consumer-preparation/recovery cut)\n482:- T287_REUSE_CONSUMER_REPAIR_04, retained-installed-consumer.mjs, prepare-retained-setup-binding.mjs, eventless View, read_only_unchanged, completeAbgEventResource, artifact_unreadable, qualification_declaration_selection_unbound, Result/J\n503:- The accepted `T287_REUSE_CONSUMER_REPAIR_04` proof covered two eventless native View calls, canonical selected-resource/Task/request/renderer preparation, immutable Task reuse, crossed/missing refusal checks, and fresh historical Result/J recovery. It used actual published transport outcomes and native selection/currentness guards. [Task 2]\n506:- Accepted scope is private component preparation plus eventless/non-advancing native consumption and controlled historical recovery. Remaining work includes Public preparation, installed known-failure/citation -> F11 -> sole AF22 -> fresh-read conservation, genuine F11 defects, exact final qualification, and RC1 publication/owner acceptance. [Task 3]\n547:- `odd_manager` owns bounded admission/read models and operator presentation; ABIogenesis owns events, replay semantics, Run truth, and liveness. The slice supplies identity-first discovery, per-Run status, bounded event pages, and lazy call detail. Key seams: `build_tenants/react_vite/src/server/abg-event-carrier-service.mjs`, `retained-run-observation-service.mjs`, `src/contracts/abg-run-observation.ts`, browser ingress validation, and `runtime/tests/test_t046_current_run_observation.mjs`. [Task 1]\n602:- ABIogenesis, code review, last 2 days of work, uncommitted-work, git status --porcelain=v1, git log --since='2 days ago', file mtimes, qualification contraction, retained-transition reuse, cold-record decoder, public readback, native workspace execution, GTL, HoG, ABG, Event Calculus, T-287\n611:- Start scope discovery with commit dates, file modification times, dated work records, and `git status` together. Relevant records included `20260923_RETAINED_TRANSITION_REUSE`, `20260923_GENERIC_DELIVERY`, `20260923_COLD_RECORD_DECODER`, `20260923_CROSS_CUT_PUBLIC_READ`, and `20260922_QUALIFICATION_CONTRACTION`. [Task 1]\n645:- STDO owns reusable validity, review, qualification, compression-fidelity, and evidence relations; ABIogenesis owns runtime events, Event Calculus/replay, worksite observations, concrete counters, threat model, and implementation mechanisms. Do not turn shared recommendations into universal runtime architecture. [Task 1]\n651:- symptom: a strategy post silently becomes standards or runtime architecture -> cause: shared method law and project-local mechanisms were conflated -> fix: keep concrete event, projection, counter, and adapter rules in ABIogenesis Product/design/requirements, and keep the post clearly uncommitted commentary until explicit adoption. [Task 1]\n699:# Task Group: ABIogenesis recovery after review-to-execution drift, selected commentary restoration, and post lookup\n701:scope: Use after an authorized ABIogenesis recovery from a rejected development cut, when restoring only selected archived commentary, or when locating the restored four-dimensional lifecycle post.\n708:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T17-35-12-O9s1-abiogenesis_review_recovery_commentary_restore_four_dimensio.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/21/rollout-2026-08-21T03-35-12-01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-30T04:56:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d, rejected dev.287 was archived and main restored to stable dev.286)\n718:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T17-35-12-O9s1-abiogenesis_review_recovery_commentary_restore_four_dimensio.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/21/rollout-2026-08-21T03-35-12-01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-30T04:56:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d, exact archival blob restoration and pushed parity verification)\n728:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T17-35-12-O9s1-abiogenesis_review_recovery_commentary_restore_four_dimensio.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/21/rollout-2026-08-21T03-35-12-01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-30T04:56:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d, current-main tracked-file lookup)\n737:- when development fails, the user prefers tagged-main recovery: branch it “for posterity/selective poaching,” reset to the last stable tag, then continue from there; preserve named stable releases such as `4.6.0-rc.3`. [Task 1]\n743:- Stable recovery pattern: archive a failed candidate under a descriptive remote branch, verify archive containment, reset `main` to the last stable immutable tag, then clean redundant branches/worktrees only with authorization. [Task 1]\n763:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T17-35-12-O9s1-abiogenesis_review_recovery_commentary_restore_four_dimensio.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/21/rollout-2026-08-21T03-35-12-01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-30T04:56:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d, timestamp-prefixed commentary navigation)\n857:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T17-35-12-O9s1-abiogenesis_review_recovery_commentary_restore_four_dimensio.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/21/rollout-2026-08-21T03-35-12-01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-30T04:56:48+00:00, thread_id=01a0203d-bee7-76e3-b8dd-c95628587d2d, review-only overlay analysis did not reach a final verdict)\n1122:- Proposed probes are the neutral sum-and-histogram categorical steel thread, uncertain-effect recovery, and bounded ordinary triage/ticket/release tasks using a common oracle and selected frames. The proposed 90-minute-per-assessor/USD-10 envelope and reported ~32,600-token scratch experiment remain proposal/exploratory evidence, not an authorized spend grant or qualification. [Task 2]\n1127:- symptom: document counts, syntax/link checks, successful maps, copied-text percentage, or URI count are called proof -> cause: mechanical evidence was substituted for semantic conservation, foundational integration, or qualification -> fix: inspect changed semantic boundaries, permissions, conditions, negative results, authority, retained distinctions, and explicit conditional foundation/work-recovery contracts. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
