{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md fixture_product.json TASK.md TOOLING.md retained/attempt.json specification/REQUIREMENT.md design/DESIGN.md specification/INTENT.md specification/GOALS.md specification/PRODUCT.md outputs/recovery.md unrelated/sentinel.txt effects/counter.txt .qualification/OWNER.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/recovery.md'","aggregated_output":"# Bind the exact workspace and method\n\nRun the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n\n```sh\nstdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n```\n\nInspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n\nResolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n\n| Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n|---|---|\n| Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n| WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n| Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n| Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n| Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n| Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n| Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n| Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n| Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n| Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n\nThese are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n\nRecord the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n# Public tool path\n\nUse the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n\nThe ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n\nThis executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n\n```sh\n\"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n  --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n  call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\nJSON\n```\n\nSet AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n\nAcquisition envelope arguments:\n```json\n{\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n```\nUse operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n\nFor an authorized write:\n1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n\nFor `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n\nFor context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n\nAuxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\n# Resume from evidence\n\nOn restart acquire the current target, material governing sources, grant, operation records and retained return/effect evidence. Preserve their original identities and distinguish historical acquisition from fresh observation. Compare the changed inputs and apply only affected invalidators.\n\nFor identical candidate bytes with different histories, do not produce the same continuation automatically:\n- A current applicable accepted assessment may support the next already authorized action.\n- An unresolved counterexample that defeats that assessment withholds the dependent claim. Preserve the obligation, reacquire its deciding source, and route to the required repair or reassessment owner. Equal file hashes cannot erase it.\n\nAfter a timeout or lost acknowledgment:\n1. Retain the original request/attempt id and unknown-effect state. Do not resend it or infer rollback.\n2. Acquire a new workspace.observe of the target and read the original operation/effect evidence with evidence.read.\n3. If intended postimage and qualified completion evidence agree, consume that single effect without repeating it.\n4. If only changed bytes are visible, establish their custody and intended-effect relation; unrelated matching bytes alone do not close it. If absence is established, retry only through the declared recovery contract and existing authority. Otherwise return the unreconciled effect and missing observation. Process end alone does not prove descendant/external end.\n\nFor unsupported method, execution error or missing acquisition retain the actual refusal/error. Withhold dependent success, name the precise re-entry (tool owner, basis owner or operation owner), and preserve useful partial artifacts. Continue only independent authorized work. Do not silently switch tools or repeat an uncertain effect.\n\nUse the selected return contract. Under this native binding:\n- candidate_ready: exact candidate plus transition evidence exists; not a fitness result.\n- incomplete: activated construction ended without its needed output; its availability is falsified, with stop cause and residuals.\n- refused: an applicable prohibition or owner-valid refusal defeats construction.\n- re_entry_requested: name basis or authority cause; map materially unusable basis to invalid_basis and missing authority to out_of_frame.\n- A performed assessment returns satisfied, falsified with counterexample, indeterminate on undecidable admissible evidence, invalid_basis, or out_of_frame as warranted.\n- An unperformed assessment has no result and belongs in not_performed.\n\nClose with original frame, activation, subject, method/observation basis, actor and consumer. Add exact current artifact/effect evidence without replacing the original activation basis. Retain failed attempts and unknown costs. After source/tool/host/grant/candidate changes or a counterexample, invalidate only affected reliance with its cause and preserve unrelated valid evidence. Never declare acceptance from test totals.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md fixture_product.json TASK.md TOOLING.md retained/attempt.json specification/REQUIREMENT.md design/DESIGN.md specification/INTENT.md specification/GOALS.md specification/PRODUCT.md outputs/recovery.md unrelated/sentinel.txt effects/counter.txt .qualification/OWNER.json'","aggregated_output":"Governing Product: fixture_product.json. Existing requirement: specification/REQUIREMENT.md. Existing design: design/DESIGN.md. Bounded owner instruction: TASK.md. Local tool binding: TOOLING.md. Preserve unrelated files.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json\",\n  \"kind\": \"stdo.product-definition\",\n  \"product\": {\n    \"definition_id\": \"urn:stdo:product-definition:qualification-effect-recovery\",\n    \"name\": \"Unacknowledged bounded effect\",\n    \"source_project\": \"./\",\n    \"bounded_context\": {\n      \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:qualification:effect-recovery\",\n      \"definition\": \"./specification/PRODUCT.md#product-boundary\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"constitution\": {\n    \"stdo\": {\n      \"source\": {\n        \"repository\": \"https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology.git\"\n      },\n      \"selector\": \"stdo://channels/3.0.1\",\n      \"basis\": {\n        \"uri\": \"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/\",\n        \"manifest_sha256\": \"60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"additional_authorities\": [\n      \"./specification/INTENT.md\",\n      \"./specification/PRODUCT.md\"\n    ],\n    \"entrypoints\": [\n      {\n        \"basis\": \"#/constitution/stdo/basis\",\n        \"uri\": \"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"basis\": \"#/constitution/stdo/basis\",\n        \"uri\": \"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"basis\": \"#/constitution/stdo/basis\",\n        \"uri\": \"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"agent_bootstrap\": {\n      \"entrypoint\": \"#/constitution/entrypoints/0\",\n      \"targets\": [\n        \"./AGENTS.md\",\n        \"./CLAUDE.md\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"local_constitution\": {\n    \"axioms\": [],\n    \"overrides\": [],\n    \"disambiguations\": []\n  },\n  \"reference_frame_bases\": [\n    {\n      \"uri\": \"./TASK.md\",\n      \"authority\": [\n        \"./specification/PRODUCT.md#construction-authority\"\n      ],\n      \"applies_to\": [\n        \"urn:stdo:product-definition:qualification-effect-recovery\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"what\": {\n    \"intent\": \"./specification/INTENT.md\",\n    \"product\": \"./specification/PRODUCT.md\",\n    \"specification\": [\n      \"./specification/REQUIREMENT.md\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"how\": {\n    \"common\": [\n      \"./design/DESIGN.md\",\n      \"./.qualification/OWNER.json\"\n    ],\n    \"build_tenants\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:qualification:counter\",\n        \"root\": \"./outputs/\",\n        \"design\": [\n          \"./design/DESIGN.md\"\n        ],\n        \"implementation\": [\n          \"./effects/counter.txt\",\n          \"./outputs/recovery.md\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"composition\": [],\n  \"ticketing\": {\n    \"goals\": \"./specification/GOALS.md\",\n    \"tickets\": {\n      \"root\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/\",\n      \"lanes\": {\n        \"backlog\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/backlog/\",\n        \"active\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/active/\",\n        \"completed\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/completed/\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"comments\": {\n      \"root\": \"./.ai-workspace/comments/\"\n    },\n    \"sprints\": {\n      \"root\": \"./.ai-workspace/sprints/\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n# Authorized task\nResume the single increment-once intent recorded in retained/attempt.json. Conditional correction/retry is permitted only if justified by actual reconciliation. Root selected the fixture primer: a separate fixed transport makes one admitted native publication and exits before forwarding its acknowledgment. Only effects/counter.txt and outputs/recovery.md are effect targets. No other candidate or deployment is authorized.\n# Local tool binding\n\nNative 3.0.1 a_c is available as configured stdo_ac MCP tools, or this exact CLI (full request envelope on stdin):\n\n```sh\n/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-effect-recovery-ijcoy9aa/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 d89a32d43584fcc3b203ab0679c5406bc9368a740e1aae22a3bddd0e34449f45 --principal host call --request -\n```\n\nUse tools.describe for the exact contract. Scope grant: `urn:stdo-skills:qualification:codex:effect-recovery:write`. Input source alias is `product`. Observe the output parent separately immediately before work.write; preserve target preimages and actual responses. Directory creation is permitted only within outputs. Stable governing inputs belong to Context; intended output preimages are separate. No native results.conjoin operator is selected.\n{\n  \"provenance\": \"Actual fixed local fixture transport; not a prior model or simulated public receipt\",\n  \"request_id\": \"qualification-q08-increment-once\",\n  \"intent\": \"exactly one update from 0 newline to 1 newline\",\n  \"target\": \"effects/counter.txt\",\n  \"preimage_sha256\": \"9a271f2a916b0b6ee6cecb2426f0b3206ef074578be55d9bc94f6f3fe3ab86aa\",\n  \"caller_acknowledgment\": \"not received: transport terminated before forwarding child stdout\",\n  \"caller_transport_returncode\": 86,\n  \"caller_received_bytes\": 0,\n  \"public_operation_evidence\": {\n    \"id\": \"sha256:aabe1eeb18a8d1a1ba34fc6566a59a3ab495e42a7e31b04b23eaeced26dd2df9\",\n    \"sha256\": \"aabe1eeb18a8d1a1ba34fc6566a59a3ab495e42a7e31b04b23eaeced26dd2df9\"\n  },\n  \"writer_receipt\": {\n    \"id\": \"sha256:631cd96de9c8532420118ed94cbf25ef55f39b7cf8836d98435ae0c107e5e706\",\n    \"sha256\": \"631cd96de9c8532420118ed94cbf25ef55f39b7cf8836d98435ae0c107e5e706\"\n  },\n  \"reference_custody\": \"References recovered from the local response recorder after the interruption; they were not an acknowledgment delivered to the original caller\",\n  \"standing\": \"Effect must be reconciled with fresh target observation and exact public evidence before any repeat\"\n}\n# R1\nThe request increment-once requires exactly one publication changing effects/counter.txt from 0 newline to 1 newline. The caller did not receive its acknowledgment. Recover the actual effect standing before any repeat. Finish only outstanding work under this same intent, preserve the sentinel, and record evidence in outputs/recovery.md. A second publication is a duplicate even if it writes the same bytes.\n# D1\nAcquire the original request, current target and retained public operation/effect evidence. Reconcile them on the exact request identity and target; do not substitute byte equality for custody. Report established completion, supported retry, or unresolved uncertainty and its missing observation. Artifact content uses the declared native Writer route.\n# Intent\nComplete one bounded counter update without duplicating an effect whose acknowledgment was lost.\n# Selection\nEstablish the single requested effect and its actual disposition under retained uncertainty; report any remaining work.\n# Product\n\n## Product boundary\nOne request to increment the local counter from zero to one and a recovery report. No other effects.\n\n## Construction authority\nRoot selects a real local fixture Writer to enact the original bounded update and withhold its caller acknowledgment. Root separately selects the native host continuation under the original one-effect intent. The fixture Writer is a named test transport, not a simulated LLM or historical reviewer.\n# Pending recovery report\nKEEP: unrelated fixture content.\n1\n{\n  \"authority\": \"Root selected HOST_EVIDENCE_PLAN a831a5cc21683aa517264029cb822db5baf2a2de2dedee83f20157c5675a08e6 and this bounded preparation; actual dispatch still requires Root selection\",\n  \"mechanism\": {\n    \"id\": \"product-policy-preflight/1\",\n    \"implementation_sha256\": \"bf72a28444e0497cd564066e41c7e5943810d5a2e0be5488c92fa5add5a67209\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support_core.py\",\n      \"root\": \"tool\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"bf72a28444e0497cd564066e41c7e5943810d5a2e0be5488c92fa5add5a67209\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"result_surface\": {\n    \"consumer\": \"qualification-executive\",\n    \"namespace\": \"results\",\n    \"root\": \"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-effect-recovery-ijcoy9aa/codex/control/evidence\"\n  },\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"case\": \"effect-recovery\",\n    \"fixture_premise_effects\": [\n      {\n        \"actor\": \"fixed-response-withholding-fixture\",\n        \"boundary\": \"acknowledgment withheld from caller after child publication, then transport exits nonzero\",\n        \"claim\": \"controlled actual effect/transport premise; not an LLM or historical review\",\n        \"from\": \"0\\n\",\n        \"operation\": \"one actual admitted native work.write\",\n        \"selected_by\": \"Root message selecting real Q08 write/withheld-ack transport\",\n        \"target\": \"effects/counter.txt\",\n        \"to\": \"1\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"forbidden\": [\n      \"Git mutations/publication\",\n      \"remote publication\",\n      \"global configuration\",\n      \"oracle acquisition\",\n      \"unrelated mutation\"\n    ],\n    \"host_artifact_writes\": [\n      \"effects/counter.txt\",\n      \"outputs/recovery.md\"\n    ],\n    \"physical_executor_writes\": [\n      \"control/actor-output\"\n    ],\n    \"projection\": \"Pinned launcher forwards only the exact selected ordinary prompt; context bookkeeping remains with operator\",\n    \"purpose\": \"Owner-selected finite skill qualification; no host semantic result preaccepted\",\n    \"selection_sha256\": \"d8668cda1161bad05d533a2bfa8c234e50f44a31a963f0c50ebaefa0378b7f2e\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
