"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"stdo_skills.json\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"4339a7dbc735052c08962154966fc13a4e30206d42ba2e80b53c6009a5008c22\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"codex/HOST.md\",\n      \"root\": \"successor\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\n      \"root\": \"method\",\n      \"selector\": {\n        \"lines\": [\n          1750,\n          1768\n        ]\n      },\n      \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\n      \"root\": \"method\",\n      \"selector\": {\n        \"lines\": [\n          1004,\n          1055\n        ]\n      },\n      \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json\",\n      \"root\": \"tool\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"resolution\": \"Root aliases require the active exact policy. Resolve method under the verified installation, common construction sources under the STDO Skills source project. Missing provenance routes do not authorize substitution.\"\n}\n\nscope: Use for the inherited-conjunction failure and Writer replay defects found after mechanically green T-008 Graphify support integration.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/a_c (rollout launched from /Users/jim); reuse_rule=safe for the E10/E11 failure shields and evidence boundary; treat hashes, test counts, and repair completion as frozen-rollout-specific.\n\n## Task 1: Reproduce and plan repair for E10/E11 residual defects, partial\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-13T02-20-42-8kWh-t008_repair_and_t287_claude_role_configuration.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T13-20-42-01a1330f-e567-7e70-886e-1de1e7c0aa9d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T05:36:00+00:00, thread_id=01a1330f-e567-7e70-886e-1de1e7c0aa9d, repair implementation remained unsealed)\n\n### keywords\n\n- T-008, Graphify, F_D, E10, E11, inherited applicable failure, Writer replay, claim marker, Product/principal/request ID, `history_incomplete`, ac_support_core.py, ac_support_effects.py\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when repairs follow independent review, preserve separate Executive/Worker/Reviewer authority and use exact write territory, closed evidence, and independent review before further edits; avoid broad churn. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- E10 occurs when an inherited optional applicable `P=falsified` result becomes an outer required `P` constraint but outer logic filters only current applicable keys. Preserve current mandatory-result ordering and evaluate inherited failures through a separate authenticated eligibility path; do not simply union inherited failures into current applicability. [Task 1]\n- E11 occurs when a Writer loses only its claim marker: a changed body/policy with the same Product/principal/request ID can receive the old success. Bind complete original request, Product/principal, and policy identity before claim/replay/recovery; missing stable owner history returns `history_incomplete`, never fresh planning or writing. [Task 1]\n- Integration-003's 273 tests/no skips, 9-file strict typing, 9 upstream checks, and 10 CLI/MCP checks are historical pre-repair evidence. The worker later reported 35 focused tests and 5-file typing, but sealed evidence, independent delta review, and final integration were absent. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
