act state, and by P4b recorded facts persist where the context does not, so the workspace is the truth surface and an actor's context a disposable account of it; current evidence corrects the account; discarding the account resets nothing | [The workspace and an actor's account](#the-workspace-and-an-actors-account) | the observations and reconciliations a resumption needs: the recovery contract, which is the resuming step's intake with the work state | 6, 9 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1439:| P5 (derived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise), P6 (independent); instance premise d | By P5 an effect of uncertain completion is undecided, and by P6 repeating an effect needs evidence that it is safe, so an effect of uncertain completion is reconciled before any repetition or dependent action; resumption does not imply idempotence | [§5](#5-work-state-and-restart) Resumption; [§3 Effects](#effects) | none | 4, 5 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1441:| P4b (derived from P0 and P2, with P0's premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable), P0 (recovered), P6 (independent); instance premise c | By P4b and P0 private working context does not survive the actor, and by P6 a reused judgment is not a new independent one, so handoff is by closed results without private working context; reuse checks exact applicability and three invalidators, a material input change (newly acquired material evidence included), a changed basis and a declared revising observation, and a domain trigger is an instance of one of them; a reused judgment does not satisfy a required independent judgment | [§7](#7-closed-result-and-reuse) | the revising observation a result declares, and its other invalidation conditions: the producer of that result | 7, 9 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1450:- Row 3, resumption and effects of uncertain completion: [§1 Construction relation](#construction-relation), Control, where resumption reacquires current reality and unknown effects are resolved before the next dependent action; [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §12 step 4](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#4-executive-evaluates-the-work-result), [§7 The executive configuration](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#the-executive-configuration), failure assumptions, and [§13 Handoff projection](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#13-handoff-projection), whose work result names each intended effect with its value, and the [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE family table](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#foundation-to-law), whose row for the effect field imports F4 for the reconciliation; [PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4 Explicit complete consumer update](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#explicit-complete-consumer-update), where an update of uncertain completion is reconciled from the presented preimages before any repetition; [SPEC_METHOD §4 Computed classification and treatment](SPEC_METHOD.md#computed-classification-and-treatment), where a retry waits on that reconciliation; [TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE Closed constraint, judgment, residual and stop kinds](TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#closed-constraint-judgment-residual-and-stop-kinds) and [Mutable-subject effect relation](TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#mutable-subject-effect-relation), where an effect whose end is not established is reconciled before any repetition; [FOUNDATIONS §4 Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse), where recovery reacquires current reality and need not erase valid work; [CONFORMANCE §4](CONFORMANCE.md#4-cases-for-method-discriminators), case CD-03, and [§5](CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage), discriminators 38 and 39.\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1458:### The workspace and an actor's account\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1490:of uncertain completion keeps the value `completion_unknown`, or its end\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1500:replay the complete history. The recovery contract that applies, which is\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1519:## 6. Cost and proportionality\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1535:uncertainty.\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1541:uncertainty over failure classification and evidence uncertainty count only\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1606:| P2 (independent), P0 (recovered); instance premise b | By P2 an obligation is justified only by its route to the outcome, and by P0 reasoning capacity is finite, so a method obligation is proportional only when the ambiguity it removes justifies the reasoning complexity it adds, and that complexity is not raw size | [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality), first three paragraphs | the justification of a constraint family: its owning law, once for the family | 6, 7 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1607:| P2 (independent), P0 (recovered), P1 (independent); instance premise b | By P2 and P0 detail is justified where it resolves alternatives the actor can hold, and by P1 a duplicate of truth is a second representation, not more truth, so a detailed symbolic design that resolves material alternatives within reasoning capacity is proportional; an addition that duplicates truth or adds reconciliation paths without reducing ambiguity is not | [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality), symbolic-design paragraph | none | 4, 6 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1608:| P2 (independent), P0 (recovered), P6 (independent); instance premise b | By P2 the method's own steps need an identified purpose, and by P6 and P0 repetition adds neither validity nor independence, so the method's own acquisition, hashing, review and evidence serve an identified need; repetition supplies neither validity nor independence | [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality), method's own execution | none | 7, 9 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1609:| P0 (recovered), P2 (independent); instance premise c | By P0 and P2 spend is part of what a finite actor's work costs the outcome, so a cost claim declares its allowance and reports spend measured under the selected execution binding, or recorded as unmeasured; costs that could conceal one another are kept apart; no universal quota follows | [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality), Cost is selected | the allowance: the activation that makes the claim; the measurement units and boundaries of the cost components: the selected execution binding, under [Resource limits](#resource-limits) | 8 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1610:| P0 (recovered), P5 (derived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise), P6 (independent), P2 (independent); instance premise d | By P0 limits bind only as declared and measured, by P5 an unmeasured consumption supports no claim of fit, and by P6 and P2 staying within a limit establishes no adequacy, so a resource limit binds only where it is declared, with its unit and measurement boundary, and no universal quota follows; consumption outside the measured boundary supports no fit; pressure on a limit never licenses omission, so the activation refines, sequences, reassigns or stops with a named value; staying within limits shows no adequacy and grants no authority | [Resource limits](#resource-limits) | the value of each limit and the units and boundaries the environment can measure: the selected execution binding, for a build tenant [SPEC_METHOD §11](SPEC_METHOD.md#11-build-tenant-binding) | 8, 7 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1611:| P2 (independent), P0 (recovered); instance premise a | By P2 delivery serves the outcome, and by P0 an actor can pursue only part of it at a time, so delivery for a product outcome is prioritised by this relation over likelihood, impact, reversibility, dependency and delayed feedback; probability waives no hard stop | [SPEC_METHOD §8](SPEC_METHOD.md#8-bounded-execution-in-this-method), outside this member | the default priority, the smallest supported product path first: SPEC_METHOD §8 | 1, 5 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1627:### Resource limits\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1681:## 7. Closed result and reuse\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1685:uncertainty and the invalidation conditions (the minimal shape is\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1750:### Transition evidence\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
