{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-effect-recovery-ijcoy9aa/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 d89a32d43584fcc3b203ab0679c5406bc9368a740e1aae22a3bddd0e34449f45 --principal host call --request - <<'AC_REQUEST_JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"recovery-source-observation-sufficiency-07\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1216,1256]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nAC_REQUEST_JSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:7f966d6a121b6b71a256b958f9b6fe690a857f30b03291e01fc2cfa705f7b590\",\"sha256\":\"7f966d6a121b6b71a256b958f9b6fe690a857f30b03291e01fc2cfa705f7b590\"},\"id\":\"recovery-source-observation-sufficiency-07\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8295b38d543f321c8a8ef1ef495a90c5f6194a23a03f538c8aa639bae6022608]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"Observation sufficiency. A checker that always decides `q_t` correctly\\nfrom π alone requires:\\n\\n```text\\nFor all s, s' in Ω:\\n  π(s) = π(s')  implies  q_t(s) = q_t(s').\\n```\\n\\nIf two admissible cases have the same observation but opposite truth\\nvalues, that observation cannot support a sound complete decision between\\nthem; further evidence, a justified narrower scope or an indeterminate\\njudgment is required. In a classical set model this condition permits a\\npredicate on the image of π; it establishes neither an executable decision\\nprocedure nor its cost. Unknown effects and unavailable observations\\nretain their distinctions from falsehood and from an evaluation that was\\nnot performed (Results) (P3, P1, P5, P6).\\n\\nWhere a representation is claimed sufficient for subsequent decisions,\\nidentify the consumer-required observations and readouts and material\\napplicability conditions, directly or by reference to the consuming contract.\\nIdentify input and policy scope and horizon where the claim depends on them.\\nRetain the standing, obligations, currentness and invalidation, causal\\nproducer and authority distinctions those consumers require. Two cases with\\nthe same representation but incompatible required decisions under those\\nfixed conditions falsify the sufficiency claim. This requires no anticipation\\nof all future uses (P1, P2, P6).\\n\\nWhen a chosen functional account claims decision preservation, define its\\nfunctions and domain: s is a state, u a permitted input under the fixed\\nconditions Γ, alpha maps states to representations, delta(s,u) is the\\nconsumer's decision, and delta_hat is that decision on representations.\\nDemonstrate `delta(s,u) = delta_hat(alpha(s),u)` on the declared domain\\n(equivalently factor delta through alpha with u held fixed). When it\\nclaims transition preservation, also demonstrate\\n`alpha(T(s,u)) ≈ T_hat(alpha(s),u)`, where T and T_hat are the state and\\nrepresentation transitions and ≈ is the declared adequacy relation, and\\ndemonstrate the declared readout preservation on\\nthat domain and horizon. Other frames preserve their consumer-required\\nrelational distinctions under the owning contracts; these equations impose\\nno universal functional model or executable decision procedure. Mandatory\\nauthority and hold distinctions remain exact where their contracts require\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1216,1256]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\",\"selected_sha256\":\"95ca7821f205977613af55fe08c4be662052b133d0d79c958c83299933ea21e5\",\"size_bytes\":2321,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1216,1256]},\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
